# Response headers for everything this Pages project serves.
#
# The router (apps/router) passes origin responses through unchanged — it sets no
# headers of its own — so whatever is declared here is exactly what a visitor gets
# on ninochavez.co.
#
# adapter-cloudflare appends its autogenerated `/photography/_app/immutable/*`
# block to this file at build time; both coexist in the deployed _headers.

# THIS FILE REACHES STATIC RESPONSES; `src/hooks.server.ts` REACHES RENDERED ONES.
# Both carry the same security headers, because neither covers everything.
#
# Cloudflare Pages applies `_headers` to static asset responses only — anything
# rendered by the Pages Function never sees it. Verified under `wrangler pages dev`:
# a `/*` block set headers on /photography/favicon.ico and on no HTML at all. That
# is why the page headers live in the hook.
#
# But the hook has the mirror-image gap: it never runs for a PRERENDERED route,
# which Pages serves as a static file. This app prerenders 404.html. Rely on the
# hook alone and that page — the one an attacker can reach on any URL they like —
# is the one page with no framing protection. So the full set is stated in both
# places rather than split by what each can reach.
#
# (The blog needs only `_headers` for this job because Astro emits it fully static.)
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Long-lived caching for content-stable static assets served under the
# /photography base path. Without this, Cloudflare Pages applies its default
# `max-age=0, must-revalidate` to non-hashed static files, forcing a
# revalidation round-trip on every visit — including the LCP hero image.

# Images (hero + other static imagery). SWR rather than `immutable` so a
# re-uploaded image under the same filename still propagates within a day.
/photography/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, stale-while-revalidate=86400

# Fonts are truly immutable (content never changes for a given file).
/photography/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Favicons. Not covered by the images rule above (they sit at the static root) and
# so were still being revalidated on every visit — 387 round trips in seven days
# for /photography/favicon-32x32.png alone, for a file that has never changed.
# SWR, not immutable, for the same reason as images: a replacement under the same
# filename still propagates within a day.
/photography/favicon*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, stale-while-revalidate=86400
